-- title:
--   Weighted centre powers are intersections of translated local centres
-- statement:
--   **Level and base data.** Fix a prime $q$, a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be, by `hH₁`, the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) — the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ — with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ which by `hK` is [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103): the subfield generated over $L$ by the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q \in \mathfrak m_A$ and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be non-zero with Laurent expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$, and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Here `chartAlgFin A K j` is the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j]$, `jChartFin` is $j$ viewed in it, `XFin` is its spectrum, and [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) is the pushout of the two chart spectra, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and closed immersion `ιFin` from `XFin`.
--
--   **Supersingular point.** Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of `chartAlgFin A K j` containing $\varpi$, and assume (`hss`) that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), that is: every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no non-zero point killed by $q$.
--
--   **The rigidity hypothesis `hArig`.** For every point $z$ of the two-chart model at which the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ (pulled back along `toBase`) lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of `XFin` with `ιFin` $y' = z$ satisfying the same supersingularity condition as `hss` (now for $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$), there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$ (the comparison with [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v - fu)$, subject to the following seven clauses, in which `toC` is the map from the stalk to its completion, `mkS` the quotient map onto $S$, and `germY` the canonical homomorphism from `chartAlgFin A K j` to the stalk at $z$ determined by $y'$ and `hy'`: (i) $e$ carries the germ of $a \in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ an automorphism of $K/L$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29), the chart algebra is $\tau$-stable; (iii) if moreover $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, then the restriction of $\tau$ to the chart algebra is congruent to the identity modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$; (iv) for such $\gamma, \tau$ with the restriction congruent to the identity modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ such that $\theta$ intertwines $e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ with the restriction of $\tau$, $\theta$ fixes the classes of constants, $\theta(X_k) \equiv \sum_i M_{ik}X_i$ modulo the square of $(X_0,X_1)$ in $S$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ik} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ik}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, $c \equiv 1 \pmod{\mathfrak m_W}$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, and $c \not\equiv 1 \pmod{\mathfrak m_W}$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; (v) a separation clause: primes $P_1, P_2$ of $S$, each omitting one of the classes of $X_0, X_1$, each containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, and containing elements with respective linear parts $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$ with $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$, have distinct contractions along $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$; (vi) a coefficient criterion: for a prime $P$ of $S$ omitting one of the classes of $X_0, X_1$, containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$ and containing an element with linear part $X_0$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$, an element $a$ of the chart algebra satisfies $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a) \in (e)^{-1}P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$; (vii) a clause on [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18): it lies in $K$ and in the chart algebra, there are $a_0 \in A$ with the difference lying in $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ whose degree-$e_0$ form takes unit values at all pairs $(a,b)$ in $W$ with $a$ or $b$ a unit and $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak m_W$, such that $e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(\mathrm{jqNModC} - a_0)))$ is the class of $h$.
--
--   **The linked witness.** Fix such data: a point $z$, the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk, a point $y'$ of `XFin` above $z$ with the supersingularity condition `hss'`, and `hy'y` : $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal} = y$. Fix furthermore a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$, $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak m_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, series $f_1, u_1, v_1$ with $u_1, v_1$ units and $f_1 \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` requires of this particular datum exactly the conjunction (i)–(vii) listed above.
--
--   **The weighted centre and the blow-up chart.** Let $\mathfrak N \subseteq S$ be the ideal generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$, and let $J'_y$ be its contraction along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$. The hypothesis `hJ` defines $J$ as the infimum, over all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and all automorphisms $\tau$ of $K/L$ with `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ` preserving the chart algebra, of the pullbacks of $J'_y$ along the restriction of $\tau$ to the chart algebra. By `hB`, $B$ is the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ obtained from `chartAlgFin A K j` by adjoining all $x \in K$ with $x\varpi_t \in J$.
--
--   **Valuation-theoretic and Drinfeld-model hypotheses.** Let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`). The hypothesis `hR1` states that the chart algebra is contained in $B$ and that $K$ is the field of fractions of $B$. The hypothesis `hR2` states that $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. The hypothesis `hR3` (five clauses) states that $W \cap L$ is the image of $A$, that $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that $y$ is the contraction of $\mathfrak m_W$ to the chart algebra, and that $W$ is obtained from $B$ by inverting the elements outside $\mathfrak m_W$. The hypothesis `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here) provides: for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$, a surjection $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel the elements of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$, compatible with $A \to k$, and equivariant for the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ through an element $c \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,\gamma, c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) acting by `hAction`, with $c \ne 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; stability of $B$ under all these level automorphisms; the statement that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ contains the translate, under some level automorphism attached to a $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, of the centre $\{b \in B : b \in \mathfrak m_W\}$; the statement that an element of $B$ all of whose translates under such automorphisms lie in $\mathfrak m_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$; and the statement that a level automorphism preserving $y$ preserves $W$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every natural number $n$,
--   $$J^{\,n} \;=\; \inf \Bigl\{\, J' \;:\; \exists\, \gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M'),\ \exists\, \tau \text{ with } \mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\ L\ q\ \zeta\ q\ (q^2M')\ H_1\ \gamma^{-1}\ K\ \tau \text{ preserving } \mathrm{chartAlgFin},\ J' = (\tau|_{\mathrm{chart}})^{-1}\bigl((J'_y)^{\,n}\bigr) \,\Bigr\},$$
--   the infimum being taken in the lattice of ideals of `chartAlgFin A K j` over exactly the same index family as in `hJ`, and $J'_y$ being as above the contraction of the ideal generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$, $X_1$ along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$. Thus the $n$-th power of the weighted centre is the intersection of the pullbacks of the $n$-th powers of the local centre, the power being formed inside the chart algebra after contraction and before pullback.
--
--   This is the multiplicativity step in the construction of the blow-up chart at a supersingular point of the integral model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$, in the variant of the argument which uses an auxiliary prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$ (a trivial-diamond condition modulo $\ell$) rather than extra full level structure, and which therefore applies for all primes $q$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.mem_weightedCentre_pow_of_eq_pow_mul_mem_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.mem_weightedCentre_pow_of_eq_pow_mul_mem_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd), where membership in powers of the weighted centre is translated into a divisibility statement on the blow-up chart.
